 ## Background
-The Standard Interval Tree for isosurface extraction was introduced by Cignoni, Marino, Montani, and Puppo [S3, book]. It was proposed as an alternative to kd-trees, which had a worst-case search time of $O(k + \sqrt{n})$ [S4, unofficial]. The method guarantees asymptotically optimal worst-case efficiency by grouping cells into a balanced binary tree based on their extreme value intervals [S2]. It is widely used in visualization handbooks as a standard method for accelerating the traversal phase of isosurface extraction [S3, book].
+The interval-tree data structure for isosurface extraction was proposed by Cignoni, Marino, Montani, and Puppo [S4, book][S5, unofficial]. It was proposed as an alternative to kd-trees, which had a worst-case search time of $O(k + \sqrt{n})$ [S5, unofficial]. The method guarantees asymptotically optimal worst-case efficiency by grouping cells into a balanced binary tree based on their extreme value intervals [S2, unofficial]. It is widely used in visualization handbooks as a standard method for accelerating the traversal phase of isosurface extraction [S3].
 
